From ba2228ce050fd8c22206ac47e0675c7bdce70320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:52:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx8mq-phanbell: Set the Bluetooth device address

HACK - do not send upstream. The address below belongs to one specific
board.

qca/nvm_00440302.bin carries the stock ROME address 00:00:00:00:5A:AD.
btqca's qca_check_bdaddr() reads the controller back, sees that same
value, and sets HCI_QUIRK_USE_BDADDR_PROPERTY. With no local-bd-address
in the devicetree hci_dev_setup_sync() then leaves public_addr empty and
flags the controller HCI_UNCONFIGURED, so hci_dev_open() returns
-EOPNOTSUPP and bluetoothd never claims it.

Setting the address from userspace with "btmgmt public-addr" is the
documented way out and it no longer works. On 7.2.7 and 7.2.9 the
controller accepts the NVM write and echoes the address back, but the
init HCI_Reset that follows is never transmitted and times out:

  Bluetooth: hci0: QCA setup on UART is completed
  Bluetooth: hci0: Opcode 0x0c03 failed: -110

The controller is then wedged in HCI_CONFIG, where every mgmt command
returns Invalid Index, including the one that would recover it. The same
sequence worked on 7.2.0, so something in the 7.2.1..7.2.9 stable range
regressed it; the commit has not been identified. Supplying the address
through the devicetree instead skips the reconfiguration entirely - the
controller is configured during its first setup and comes up with a
single firmware load.

The value is the ethernet MAC plus one, which is what the vendor OS
assigns: Mendel's patched hciattach reads the address out of
/etc/bluetooth/.bt_nv.bin and injects it into the NVM before download,
and on this board that file holds 02 00 06 6d a4 b1 5c d9 7c - NVM tag 2,
length 6, 7C:D9:5C:B1:A4:6D, against eth0's 7C:D9:5C:B1:A4:6C.

The real fix is for the bootloader to fill local-bd-address in from the
fuses, the way board/sunxi/board.c bluetooth_dt_fixup() does. That needs
LibreELEC's own u-boot on the board, which currently boots the vendor
U-Boot 2019.04.1.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
index 21321d7fd12a..4e8e79205526 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
@@ -513,6 +513,7 @@ bluetooth {
 		pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_bt>;
 		enable-gpios = <&gpio3 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		clocks = <&pmic>;
+		local-bd-address = [6d a4 b1 5c d9 7c];
 	};
 };
 
-- 
